---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Licence & attribution — Essentia"
  description="Everything created for Essentia is free for any use. Third-party material is excluded and remains under its owners' terms."
  breadcrumb={[
    { label: 'Archive', href: base },
    { label: 'Licence & attribution' },
  ]}
>
  <article class="page-shell legal-copy">
    <h1>Licence &amp; attribution</h1>

    <h2>What you may freely use</h2><p>
      Everything created for this project — the card designs, the rules and card
      text, the renders, the code, the documentation, and this website — is free
      for anyone to use, modify, and redistribute for any purpose, including
      commercially. No permission is needed, no attribution is required, and no
      fee applies. The project waives its rights in this material as far as the
      law allows, equivalent to a
      <a
        href="https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/"
        rel="noopener noreferrer">CC0 1.0 public-domain dedication</a
      >. The full dedication text ships as the <code>LICENSE</code> file in the repository.
    </p>

    <h2>What is excluded</h2><p>
      The grant above covers only material created for this project. It does
      <strong>not</strong> cover third-party material, which remains under its own
      owners' terms and is explicitly excluded:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Yu-Gi-Oh! card names, characters, and the official source records this
        project adapts from — Konami and their respective rights holders.
      </li>
      <li>
        Magic: The Gathering terminology and mana symbols — Wizards of the
        Coast.
      </li>
      <li>
        Imported land artwork reproduced for proxy printing — the original
        artists and their publishers.
      </li>
    </ul><p>
      Essentia is an independent, unofficial fan design project. It is not
      produced, endorsed, or approved by Konami or Wizards of the Coast. Nothing
      here grants you rights in their trademarks or artwork, and reusing this
      project's material does not transfer any such rights to you.
    </p>

    <h2>Source-backed cards</h2><p>
      Published text comes from English folder-form Magic Set Editor projects in
      this repository. Card pages expose an allowlisted public data shape;
      editor notes, local paths, and unknown source fields are never public.
    </p>

    <h2>Artwork and renders</h2><p>
      Canonical card renders are preserved in source projects. Public copies are
      regenerated without embedded source metadata. Publication remains subject
      to project asset approval and withdrawal records; withdrawing an asset
      removes it from future website output but cannot erase public Git history
      or existing clones.
    </p>

    <h2>Immutable release history</h2><p>
      ALPHA, BETA, and Release packages preserve exact card versions, canonical
      render hashes, aggregate manifests, and release metadata. They document
      published history; editable draft projects remain card-content source.
    </p>

    <h2>Brand marks</h2><p>
      The Essentia wordmark and letter mark are original project assets, created
      for this project. They are not Konami or Wizards of the Coast material.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
